<!-- A member of the full stack's local cluster (conf/full-stack/README.md; plans/Edge-Node2.md §3): every member runs
    this conf, on one external database. The cluster holds the apps and the data and is the PASS authority of the sites
    the edge cluster serves. It is conf/local-cluster/MoquiPooledConf.xml with an edge cluster in the edge node's place
    and a front node before that: that conf's comments on the shared database, the secrets, admission, balancing,
    work from the pool and draining hold here as they are, and this one says what differs. Use the Enterprise package
    (--enterprise), as for any cluster, with the apps (mr-boss brings mr-mantle). -->
<moqui-conf xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://moqui.org/xsd/moqui-conf-3.xsd">
    <default-property name="instance_purpose" value="production"/>

    <!-- The shared database and .env, as in conf/local-cluster: entity_ds_* and the secrets the first member makes the
        same on every member, cluster_base_url each member's own, runtime/db never copied. -->
    <default-property name="entity_ds_db_conf" value="postgres"/>
    <default-property name="cluster_transport" value=""/>
    <default-property name="cluster_protocol" value=""/>

    <!-- The edge pairing: made once, on one member, with the edge cluster (System › Edge Node, Pair with an edge node, at
        the edge cluster's own name, at the members' own addresses, or at an edge member's link name, which the front
        passes through to that member, once it has a certificate). It writes edge_node_url,
        edge_node_key, edge_node_pin, edge_node_id and edge_node_pairing; copy them with the rest of .env to every
        member. Each member then links to every live edge member, at each one's link name through the front, and keeps
        the list in runtime/db/edge_members. The edge members balance the cluster's work over its live members, and
        the queue, delegated calls, replication, mail, chat, calls, phones and PASS go over this pairing.
        With edge members (node_role edge, which forward no web access), a second pairing, with the front (System › Edge
        Node, the same Pair flow: the Pair screen shows the role front, and the pairing goes there): front_node_url,
        front_node_key, front_node_pin and front_node_id, copied to every member as well. The wizard then sends the host
        names and XMPP domain to the front, and the mail domains, chat bridges and PASS sites to the edge cluster; the
        front balances the names over this cluster's members directly. With front_edge members there is no second
        pairing: the members forward the names. -->

    <!-- The PASS authority (mr-pass's docs/Deployment.md, Full stack): the wizard's PASS step writes pass_edge_client
        (edge), pass_client_edge_sites and pass_client_edge_callback, the edge cluster as a PASS client with no secret,
        which the link authenticates. Every edge member calls the authority down its own link, balanced over the live
        members, sticky by the sign-in in progress. Create each site and bind its hosts and mounts here
        (mantle.public.SiteServices.create#Site, store#Mounts), the same hosts as the edge members' public-site
        bindings. The authority needs no public address, open port or client secret. -->

    <!-- Web access: the client's address comes over the link, as with one edge node, so no webapp_trusted_proxies. The
        apps' own names (erp.example.com) are given by the wizard: terminate on the front (its certificate there, sticky
        by the session cookie), or passthrough (the certificate in runtime/cert on each member, the same files). -->

    <!-- Mail out through the edge cluster: an EmailServer EDGE with smtpHost edge:, which the wizard sets: each message goes
        up once, whichever member sends it, and an edge member delivers it from its own address. Calls and phones: the edge members' media nodes and SIP, a row each that
        the links keep. -->

    <entity-facade crypt-pass="${entity_ds_crypt_pass}" query-stats="true"/>
</moqui-conf>
